WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.274
Now let's create a simple grouped summary The goal
is one row

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:11.031
per diagnosis with a count of admissions inside each
diagnosis The

00:00:11.045 --> 00:00:15.426
diagnosis column defines the groups and COUNT
calculates a measure within each

00:00:15.439 --> 00:00:21.378
group Before running the query predict which
diagnosis will have the largest

00:00:21.405 --> 00:00:27.664
count Then run it in the browser and inspect the
result Notice

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:31.348
that the original admission rows have been collapsed
into a smaller summary

00:00:31.374 --> 00:00:36.495
table We no longer see individual admission IDs
because the output grain

00:00:36.508 --> 00:00:42.037
is diagnosis If you copy this query into pgAdmin try

00:00:42.051 --> 00:00:47.211
adding ORDER BY admission count descending Sorting
does not change the grouping

00:00:48.145 --> 00:00:51.395
It simply makes the largest groups easier to
identify
